   "Halcyon-negotiator": "collaborating"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting of every thermal incident within 24 hours, with no serious/minor split, which directly addresses the unreported-incident problem on both sides. S2 keeps the 5% benchmark and gives customers numeric rates, but removes any obligation to stop sales above it, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 replaces any automatic recall at 8 per 100k with regulator discretion and open-ended corrective alternatives, which favours Halcyon's Ember 8; S3's 6-year retrofit window and S4's 36-month start both fall inside the acceptable ranges and protect each company's red line."
 },
